  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Processes",
      "items": [
        "One scheduler process (make run-background-jobs, scheduler.py): APScheduler runs every job of this page in its threads; one container (the workers VM, preprod-app on preprod)",
        "The ES syncer is a second, long-running process (make run-syncer): it consumes the Redis queue, it is not scheduled",
        "The store of each harvester (avalanche_bulletins/store.py, weather.py) runs inside run_source, in the transaction that records the source"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The harvest tick",
      "items": [
        "Every minute (APScheduler, max_instances=1, coalesce): every 10 min sync the sources, then claim the due ones (next_run_at <= now) with FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED; the claim moves next_run_at 10 min later (lease)",
        "At most 60 sources a tick, and requests_per_minute for a harvester with a quota (Météo-France: 40)",
        "Lanes by host: 4 worker threads, at most 2 lanes a host, so a service never gets more than 2 requests at once",
        "304 or same SHA-256: nothing stored. New content: payload kept gzipped, then harvester.store(session) in the same transaction as the source state",
        "Errors: error_count + 1, backoff 15 min doubled up to 4 h; success: next_run_at = policy.next_run (publication windows 07:00-10:00, 15:30-19:00 Paris)"
      ]
    },
    {
